  "name": "Example: Identifying \"Or\" Inequalities Given on Number Lines",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151668/assets/7ae1311495d3fcb290bdf3f4b303224415e2e55c5ae1af8a82efd1f3aa2572b4.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?",
  "worked_solution": "The red rays contain all values less than $-4$ or greater than $-1.$ In addition, \n\n- the open circle at $-4$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $-4,$ and\n\n- the closed circle at $-1$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-1.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x <    -4$ or $x \\geq -1.$",
